        {
          "id": 1075361350,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Old GCC (or whatever compiler generated what's in tools/abi-dumps) debug symbols vs. GCC 11.2.0 debug symbols, even with both generating DWARF 4?\n\nMight new GCC be generating debugging symbols in such a way that abi-dump sees `etype_vals[]` being an array of a specific size, rather than an array of unknown size?\n\nOr might this be a difference between versions of abi-dump?",
